By using the keyboard. 

Hold shift and use the arrow keys to highlight text.

Copy is control+c
Paste is control+v
Cut is control+x

Find is control+f

Undo is control+z
Redo is control+y

If you want to see them all (there's so many) you can press control+e (this lets you use comm-ands which you will see on the bottom) and type "help defaultkeys". You can just scroll down and  see the list. Press control+g to quit it.


When you're on your homepage and decide to make a new file, you'll notice it asks if you w-ant a blank or MLA format file. Blank is blank and MLA format is pretty interesting. If youchoose MLA format, it'll make a file ending in ".txt". When you open it it'll look like an interesting format, but just fill it out normally. Put your full name, instructor name, yadayada. It's simple to use, just keep the formatting the same, the spaces between each line are essential so make sure they stay. You can make as many body paragraphs as you want just make sure to put a space between them. When you're done, exit the file and while its high-lighted, press 'c' and it'll make a duplicate of that file that ends in ".docx". You wont be able to open those files on this device.

Thats the basics, you should be able to figure out the rest. Good luck
